# =====================================================================
# Insight Finder — environment template
# =====================================================================
# Two audiences, one file:
#   1. FRONTEND (Vite)      -> copy to `.env` / `.env.local` at the repo root.
#   2. EDGE FUNCTIONS (Deno)-> these are SECRETS in the Supabase project's
#      secret store. They are never read from a local `.env`.
#
# EVERY line below is commented out on purpose. Copying this file to `.env`
# changes nothing: the app keeps its built-in defaults. Uncomment only what
# you mean to set. Never commit a populated `.env` (all `.env.*` variants are
# git-ignored; only this template is tracked).
#
# Defaults quoted here were read from source (supabase/functions/osint-agent/
# env.ts, runtime-policy.ts, and the module named beside each switch). They
# drift. The deployed build is the authority: GET .../osint-agent?health=1
# (build SHA + `checks.*`). Edge code deploys are a separate manual step; see
# CLAUDE.md and .claude/skills/edge-deploy/SKILL.md.
#
# Kill switches below all follow one rule: UNSET = the feature stays ON.
# Set `NAME=true` to turn it OFF on the running build, with no deploy.
# =====================================================================


# ---- 1. Frontend (Vite; values are public and ship in the client bundle) --
# Read at BUILD time: changing these needs a rebuild/redeploy.
#
# ⚠️ UNSET IS NOT "OFFLINE". src/integrations/supabase/client.ts falls back to
# baked-in defaults that point at the LIVE hosted backend, so `npm run dev`
# with no `.env` talks to production data. To work against your own project,
# set BOTH of the next two. To work with no backend at all, use the harness:
#   npx vite --config vite.harness.config.ts      # http://127.0.0.1:5174
#
# Supabase Dashboard > Project Settings > API
# VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://<project-id>.supabase.co
# VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=<anon / publishable key from the dashboard>
# VITE_SUPABASE_PROJECT_ID=<project-id>
#
# "true" shows the Google sign-in button (needs a Google client id/secret
# configured in Supabase). Default: hidden, email/password only.
# VITE_ENABLE_GOOGLE_OAUTH=true
#
# "true" masks breach values behind click-to-reveal. Default: values render in
# the clear (owner decision while the product is in development). The
# minor-safety redaction is separate and absolute in both modes.
# VITE_MASK_BREACH_VALUES=true
#
# "true" restores the pre-CO_RECORD identity clusters and graph. Default: off.
# VITE_CO_RECORD_LINKAGE_DISABLED=true


# ---- 2. Platform-injected (the Supabase edge runtime provides these) ------
# Do NOT set them. Listed so the full set of names the functions read is here.
# SERVICE_ROLE_KEY bypasses row-level security: never put it in the frontend.
# SUPABASE_URL=
# SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=


# ---- 3. Orchestrator (the model that drives a run) ------------------------
# Selection lives in supabase/functions/osint-agent/orchestrator_select.ts.
# ORCHESTRATOR_PROVIDER pins the primary. Recognised values:
#   deepseek | minimax | grok (or xai) | anthropic (or claude)
# An unrecognised value, or a pin whose key is not set, is ignored and the
# automatic order applies: the DeepSeek slot if configured, else MiniMax, else
# xAI Grok. Anthropic is never chosen automatically; it is primary only by an
# explicit pin, and otherwise serves as the backup. (`lovable` is NOT a valid
# pin, whatever the older comment in env.ts says.)
# Production pins the DeepSeek slot to Z.AI GLM, with Anthropic as the backup
# (a failed START falls back to Anthropic; never mid-run). Re-pinning
# production is an owner decision: see CLAUDE.md.
# ORCHESTRATOR_PROVIDER=
#
# -- Primary: the "deepseek" slot. It is an OpenAI-compatible endpoint, so it
# -- can point at any compatible vendor with secrets alone.
# GLM_API_KEY wins over DEEPSEEK_API_KEY when it is non-empty.
# GLM_API_KEY=
# DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=
# Default https://api.deepseek.com/v1. For Z.AI GLM use https://api.z.ai/api/paas/v4
# DEEPSEEK_BASE_URL=
# Default deepseek-v4-pro. For Z.AI GLM use glm-5.2
# DEEPSEEK_ORCHESTRATOR_MODEL_ID=
# disabled | enabled | auto (default: decided from the model id). GLM-5.3 models
# force thinking on and reject "disabled"; see lib/glm-thinking.ts.
# DEEPSEEK_THINKING_MODE=
# Default low.
# DEEPSEEK_REASONING_EFFORT=
# "true" runs the provider preflight probe on every request (default: skipped
# when the result could not change routing).
# DEEPSEEK_PREFLIGHT_ALWAYS=true
# "true" lets a failed preflight pivot the run onto gemini-direct. Default off:
# that pivot finished 0 of 16 runs when measured (lib/preflight-pivot.ts).
# GEMINI_PREFLIGHT_PIVOT_ENABLED=true
#
# -- Backup: Anthropic (anthropic-orchestrator.ts).
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# Default claude-sonnet-5, on purpose: Sonnet 5.5 / Opus 5.5 / Fable 5.1 reject
# the forced tool_choice the finalize phases need. Do not "upgrade" this.
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL_ID=
# ANTHROPIC_THINKING=
# ANTHROPIC_EFFORT=
# Per-run caps. Defaults 1500000 input tokens and 2000000 micro-USD ($2).
# ANTHROPIC_RUN_INPUT_TOKEN_BUDGET=
# ANTHROPIC_RUN_COST_CEILING_MICRO_USD=
#
# -- Alternates (working, not primary).
# MINIMAX_API_KEY=
# Default MiniMax-M2.7
# MINIMAX_ORCHESTRATOR_MODEL_ID=
# XAI_API_KEY=
# Default grok-4.3
# GROK_ORCHESTRATOR_MODEL_ID=
# LOVABLE_API_KEY=
# "true" opts in to the Lovable AI gateway as a fallback. Default: off.
# ALLOW_LOVABLE_FALLBACK=true
# Default google/gemini-2.5-flash
# LOVABLE_FALLBACK_MODEL_ID=
#
# -- Gemini (grounded search and vision).
# GEMINI_API_KEY=
# Default gemini-2.5-flash
# GEMINI_FALLBACK_MODEL_ID=
# Defaults to GEMINI_FALLBACK_MODEL_ID.
# GEMINI_VISION_MODEL_ID=


# ---- 4. Health probe ------------------------------------------------------
# Gates the paid ?probe=1 path (checked against the x-probe-secret header).
# Unset = ?probe=1 is rejected (fails closed). Plain ?health=1 is public and
# is NOT free of provider calls: it pings the orchestrator providers.
# OSINT_AGENT_PROBE_SECRET=


# ---- 5. Dark switches (default OFF; the shipped behaviour is "off") --------
# Turning any of these on changes production data or spend. Read the module
# named beside each one first.
#
# Finding synthesis sweep (finding-synthesis-sweep.ts). Accepts true or 1.
# Forward path, then the historical backfill (a WRITE into closed cases), then
# a dry run that computes and reports but writes nothing.
# FINDING_SYNTHESIS_ENABLED=true
# FINDING_SYNTHESIS_BACKFILL_ENABLED=true
# FINDING_SYNTHESIS_DRY_RUN=true
#
# Tool-cache sweep (cache-sweep.ts). Accepts 1, true, yes or on. ENABLED
# DELETES production rows; do not enable it before the payload store exists
# (CLAUDE.md). Use DRY_RUN to measure the backlog first.
# CACHE_SWEEP_ENABLED=true
# CACHE_SWEEP_DRY_RUN=true
#
# GRAPH_PIVOTS_ENABLED=true
# CLUSTER_LEGACY_NEEDS_REVIEW_CONTRADICTION=true
# HEALTH_MAINTENANCE_ALWAYS=true
# Adds a bounded, redacted body excerpt to the stream-error LOG LINE only;
# nothing persisted changes.
# STREAM_ERROR_BODY_DETAIL=true


# ---- 6. Run limits and budgets (runtime-policy.ts) ------------------------
# Defaults shown. The cap stays bounded on purpose: an unbounded run runs out
# of wall-clock instead of budget and dies in a worse place (CLAUDE.md).
# MAX_TOTAL_TOOL_CALLS_PER_RUN=30
# MAX_PAID_CALLS_PER_RUN=12
# MAX_PARALLEL_TOOLS=3
# MAX_SAME_TOOL_CALLS_PER_RUN=16
# STOP_ON_BUDGET_EXHAUSTED=true
# MIN_START_GAP_MS=100
# LeakCheck quota guard (lib/leakcheck-guard.ts). Defaults 3 and 20.
# LEAKCHECK_MAX_PER_INVESTIGATION=3
# LEAKCHECK_QUOTA_RESERVE=20


# ---- 7. Breach-data display (server side) ---------------------------------
# DEFAULT IS ON (raw breach values), by the owner's decision while the product
# is in development. Setting "false" gives masked-by-default, NOT
# click-to-reveal. Surfaced at /health as `reveal_breach_data`. A serus reveal
# also needs a SERUS_API_KEY that carries the `darkweb:reveal` scope.
# REVEAL_BREACH_DATA=false


# ---- 8. Provider keys -----------------------------------------------------
# Every key is optional; a tool whose key is unset skips itself and says so.
# A 403 is not proof a key is dead: measure outcomes before rotating anything.
#
# Breach and identity
# STOLENTAX_API_KEY=       # stolen.tax breach + footprint
# LEAKCHECK_API_KEY=       # LeakCheck Pro v2 corroboration
# DEEPFIND_API_KEY=        # DeepFind.Me reverse-email, social, specialty
# OATHNET_API_KEY=         # OathNet breach + stealer logs
# SYNAPSINT_API_KEY=       # Synapsint aggregator (cut: dead in prod)
# OSINTNOVA_API_KEY=       # OSINTNova (Bosint) email + phone
# INDICIA_API_KEY=         # api.indicia.app; six endpoints only, by policy
# SOCIALFETCH_API_KEY=     # TikTok / Instagram / Twitter / Facebook profiles
# CORDCAT_API_KEY=         # Discord snowflake OSINT
# HUNTER_API_KEY=          # Hunter.io email verification + finding
# INTELBASE_API_KEY=       # IntelBase (hard-coded OFF in env.ts)
# HIBP_API_KEY=            # Have I Been Pwned v3
# SERUS_API_KEY=           # Serus darkweb scan (metered)
# PEOPLEDATALABS_API_KEY=  # People Data Labs person enrichment
# RAPIDAPI_KEY=            # RapidAPI email breach search
# RAPIDAPI_BREACH_HOST=    # default email-breach-search.p.rapidapi.com
# RAPIDAPI_BREACH_PATH=    # default /rapidapi/search-email/
# RAPIDAPI_ALL_BREACHES_PATH=  # default /rapidapi/all-breaches
# RANSOMWARELIVE_API_KEY=  # ransomware.live API-pro (the free API is retired)
#
# Infrastructure, network and corporate
# VIRUSTOTAL_API_KEY=      # VirusTotal v3
# URLSCANNER_API_KEY=      # URLScanner.online private scans
# FOFA_API_KEY=            # FOFA internet-asset search (points-metered)
# IPGEOLOCATION_API_KEY=   # IP geolocation
# IPQUALITYSCORE_API_KEY=  # IP / email / phone reputation
# GEOSEER_API_KEY=         # GeoSeer AI image geolocation (paid per call)
# OPENCORPORATES_API_KEY=  # OpenCorporates search (keyless calls get 401)
# OPSIS_API_KEY=           # Opsis search and results
#
# Web search, scrape and code
# EXA_API_KEY=             # Exa neural + keyword search
# JINA_API_KEY=            # Jina Reader (works unauthenticated)
# FIRECRAWL_API_KEY=       # Firecrawl (disabled in code: credits exhausted)
# PERPLEXITY_API_KEY=      # Perplexity Sonar
# GITHUB_API_TOKEN=        # GitHub code + user lookups
# GITHUB_TOKEN=            # alternate name for the same
# OSINT_NAVIGATOR_API_KEY= # OSINT Navigator tool recommendation
# (GEMINI_API_KEY is in section 3.)


# ---- 9. Legacy-restore switches (default OFF = the current behaviour) ------
# Set "true" ONLY to put the previous behaviour back on a running build.
# true = legacy: a dropped browser connection persists a partial transcript
# and ends the run.
# PERSIST_ON_CLIENT_CANCEL=true
# Restores the pre-2026-09-24 SSRF checker (IPv4 private ranges + ::1 only).
# SSRF_GUARD_LEGACY=true


# ---- 10. Kill switches (UNSET = feature stays ON) -------------------------
# Set `NAME=true` to turn the feature OFF with no deploy. Most are
# integrity controls. Flip one only to recover from a fault, and say so in the
# incident log. Two need extra care:
#   RUN_LEASE_DISABLED        CLAUDE.md records production with this set true
#                             (the run lease is deployed but off). Changing it
#                             needs the owner's authorization.
#   PROMOTION_QUARANTINE_DISABLED  true restores the old dispatch refusal for
#                             quarantined selectors.
# ANALYST_AUTHORITY_STRIP_DISABLED=true
# ANTHROPIC_FALLBACK_DISABLED=true
# ANTHROPIC_PROMPT_REPAIR_DISABLED=true
# ARCHIVE_ORIGIN_RULE_DISABLED=true
# BREACH_EXPOSURE_GUARD_DISABLED=true
# BREACH_ORIGIN_CAP_DISABLED=true
# CLUSTER_BOOKKEEPING_INERT_DISABLED=true
# CLUSTER_URL_HANDLE_TOKENS_DISABLED=true
# CONTRADICTION_CLAIM_FILTER_DISABLED=true
# CROSS_CASE_REVIEWS_DISABLED=true
# DEAD_TARGET_MEMORY_DISABLED=true
# DISPATCH_SELECTOR_ALIASES_DISABLED=true
# EXACT_BOOLEAN_REPAIR_DISABLED=true
# HISTORICAL_MEMORY_MARK_DISABLED=true
# HISTORY_LABEL_DISABLED=true
# INDICIA_MISSING_FIRST_NAME_DISABLED=true
# INPUT_COERCION_DISABLED=true
# MALFORMED_JSON_REPAIR_DISABLED=true
# MEMORY_AS_SOURCE_DISABLED=true
# MEMORY_AUTHORITY_WORDING_DISABLED=true
# MEMORY_INPUT_NORMALIZATION_DISABLED=true
# NEGATIVE_LOOKUP_DISABLED=true
# NEGATIVE_QUALIFIER_CLASS_DISABLED=true
# NEXT_PIVOT_BRIEF_DISABLED=true
# OPSIS_CREDIT_HINT_DISABLED=true
# OPSIS_DISABLED=true
# OPSIS_FINALIZE_COLLECT_DISABLED=true
# OPSIS_RESULTS_HINT_DISABLED=true
# OPSIS_SEARCH_GUARD_DISABLED=true
# OPSIS_START_CLASSIFY_DISABLED=true
# PROMOTION_QUARANTINE_DISABLED=true
# PROMPT_BUDGET_HARD_CEILING_DISABLED=true
# PROVIDER_AUTH_PRIOR_DISABLED=true
# PROVIDER_BUSY_QUEUE_DISABLED=true
# RECORD_ARTIFACTS_INPUT_COMPACT_DISABLED=true
# RECORD_NAME_QUARANTINE_DISABLED=true
# REJECTED_CLUSTER_SWEEP_DISABLED=true
# RUN_END_LOG_DISABLED=true
# RUN_LEASE_DISABLED=true
# SEED_ACCOUNT_ID_DISABLED=true
# SERUS_NAME_FILTER_DISABLED=true
# SOCIALFETCH_COERCION_DISABLED=true
# SOURCE_ORIGIN_RULES_DISABLED=true
# TIMING_TELEMETRY_DISABLED=true
# TOOL_CACHE_VERSION_DISABLED=true
# TOOL_INPUT_FAILURE_LOG_DISABLED=true
# TOOL_INPUT_OBJECT_REPAIR_DISABLED=true
# USER_SUPPLIED_STATUS_CEILING_DISABLED=true


# ---- 11. Distributed rate limiter (optional) ------------------------------
# Set BOTH to upgrade the per-user limiter from in-memory (per instance) to a
# cross-instance Upstash counter (ratelimit.ts). Without them the function
# falls back to the in-memory cap and keeps working.
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=https://<instance>.upstash.io
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=


# ---- Operator notes -------------------------------------------------------
# 1. A key that was committed, pasted into chat, or put in a doc is
#    compromised. Rotate it at the provider, then update the secret.
# 2. Edge secrets live in the Supabase project's secret store. Changing a
#    secret needs no code change. Deploying edge code is a separate manual
#    step with its own gate (CLAUDE.md, edge-deploy skill). Do not use
#    `supabase functions deploy`.
# 3. After any secret or deploy change, check ?health=1 for the build SHA and
#    the relevant `checks.*` key instead of assuming it landed.
# 4. Frontend `.env` changes need a Vite rebuild and redeploy.
